  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A block of mass &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&#39; (as shown in figure) moving with kinetic energy <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>E</mi></math> compresses a spring through a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> when, its speed is halved. The value of spring constant of used spring will be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo></math>_____.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/f9ed0b74-c6e4-4159-a921-4b9b3ba1163a-image.png\" style=\"width: 130px; height: 99px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "24",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Using work <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math> energy theorem</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>net</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>E</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mi>E</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>E</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn><mi>E</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Thus, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
